{
  "info": {
    "name": "Nahuat API",
    "description": "Collection for the Nahuat API (NestJS). URI-versioned under /api/v1; health opts out at /api/health.\n\n## Environments\nPick an environment (top-right) rather than editing collection variables — every URL is driven by `{{baseUrl}}`/`{{healthBase}}`:\n- **Nahuat — Local** → http://localhost:3001\n- **Nahuat — Staging** → https://api.staging.nahuat.com\n\n## Auth\nA global JwtAuthGuard protects every route unless marked public. Tokens are real Auth0 access tokens (RS256, verified via JWKS against the tenant) — there is no local/HS256 bypass (ADR 13).\n\nThe token carries only `sub`. Since 2026-08-24 the API resolves the platform user id and role from its own database on every request, so a role change takes effect immediately rather than at the next login, and a deactivated account is refused on its next request with USER_DEACTIVATED. Roles are ranked USER < CONTRIBUTOR < ADMIN.\n\n- **Public** routes (dictionary reads, GET /dialects, health) need no token and work in every environment.\n- **Authed** routes read `{{token}}` as a Bearer token. Log into the web app for the environment you are targeting and copy the access token it sends to the API.\n\nFill `entryId`/`translationId`/`dialectId`/`slug` from a browse/list response.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3001/api/v1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "webBaseUrl",
      "value": "",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "healthBase",
      "value": "http://localhost:3001/api",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "entryId",
      "value": "REPLACE_WITH_ENTRY_ID",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "translationId",
      "value": "REPLACE_WITH_TRANSLATION_ID",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "dialectId",
      "value": "REPLACE_WITH_DIALECT_ID",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "slug",
      "value": "takat",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{healthBase}}/health",
              "host": ["{{healthBase}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Liveness probe (what the ALB polls). Public, version-neutral."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{healthBase}}/health/ready",
              "host": ["{{healthBase}}"],
              "path": ["health", "ready"]
            },
            "description": "Readiness probe (DB connectivity). Public, version-neutral."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Session",
      "description": "Getting a token. /auth/access-token is mounted on the WEB app by the Auth0 SDK ({{webBaseUrl}}), not on the API ({{baseUrl}}) — the API never issues tokens, it only verifies them.\n\nIt authorises by SESSION COOKIE, so Postman needs the cookie the browser holds. Sign in at {{webBaseUrl}}, then copy the session cookie into Postman's Cookies manager for that domain (Cookies, under the Send button). Once it is there this request works and re-running it refreshes an expired token.\n\nIf you would rather not manage cookies, open {{webBaseUrl}}/auth/access-token in the browser and paste the `token` value into the environment by hand.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get access token → saves {{token}}",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{webBaseUrl}}/auth/access-token",
              "host": ["{{webBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "access-token"]
            },
            "description": "Returns { token, expiresAt } for the signed-in session and writes `token` into the active environment, so every authed request in this collection picks it up.\n\nThe token carries only `sub`. Your rank comes from your user row, which the API reads on every request — so changing a role in the database takes effect immediately and does NOT need a new token."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Writes the token into the active environment so the",
                  "// collection-level Bearer auth ({{token}}) picks it up.",
                  "let body;",
                  "try {",
                  "    body = pm.response.json();",
                  "} catch (e) {",
                  "    body = null;",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('200 with a token', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(body && body.token, 'no token in response').to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 401 || pm.response.code === 302) {",
                  "    // No session cookie, or it expired. Postman does not follow the",
                  "    // login redirect usefully — sign in in the browser first.",
                  "    console.log('Not signed in. Sign in at the web app, then copy the session cookie into Postman.');",
                  "} else if (body && typeof body.token === 'string') {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('token', body.token);",
                  "    const expiresAt = body.expiresAt ? new Date(body.expiresAt * 1000).toISOString() : 'unknown';",
                  "    console.log('Saved {{token}}. Expires: ' + expiresAt);",
                  "} else {",
                  "    // Leave the old token alone rather than blanking it: a transient",
                  "    // failure should not also log you out of every other request.",
                  "    console.log('No token saved; the previous {{token}} is unchanged.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dictionary — reads (public)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Browse entries",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries?page=1&limit=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20"
                },
                {
                  "key": "type",
                  "value": "WORD",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "WORD | EXPRESSION (PHRASE is rejected — lesson-only)"
                },
                {
                  "key": "partOfSpeech",
                  "value": "NOUN",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "NOUN|VERB|ADJECTIVE|ADVERB|PRONOUN|PARTICLE|PREPOSITION|CONJUNCTION|OTHER"
                },
                {
                  "key": "dialectCode",
                  "value": "common",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "isPublished",
                  "value": "true",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "CONTRIBUTOR+ only; ignored for public requests"
                },
                {
                  "key": "locale",
                  "value": "en",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "es (default) | en — resolves gloss/example language"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Paginated browse. Public. Returns WORD/EXPRESSION only."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Search entries",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries/search?q=takat",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries", "search"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "q",
                  "value": "takat",
                  "description": "required; pg_trgm fuzzy match"
                },
                {
                  "key": "type",
                  "value": "WORD",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "dialectCode",
                  "value": "common",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Fuzzy search. `q` is required (400 without it). Public."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Entry by slug",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries/by-slug/{{slug}}?locale=es",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries", "by-slug", "{{slug}}"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "locale",
                  "value": "es",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Canonical addressing by slug (accent-folded nawatContent). Public."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Entry by id",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries/{{entryId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries", "{{entryId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Full detail by id. Public."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dictionary — writes (CONTRIBUTOR / ADMIN)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create entry (CONTRIBUTOR)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"nawatContent\": \"kunet\",\n  \"type\": \"WORD\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries"]
            },
            "description": "Create a headword only (translations added separately). imageUrl optional. Requires CONTRIBUTOR."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create full entry (CONTRIBUTOR)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"nawatContent\": \"kunet\",\n  \"type\": \"WORD\",\n  \"translations\": [\n    {\n      \"dialectCode\": \"common\",\n      \"contentEs\": \"niño | bebé\",\n      \"contentEn\": \"child | baby\",\n      \"partOfSpeech\": \"NOUN\",\n      \"phonetic\": \"[ˈkunet]\",\n      \"exampleNawat\": \"Ne kunet kochi.\",\n      \"exampleEs\": \"El niño duerme.\",\n      \"exampleEn\": \"The child sleeps.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries/full",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries", "full"]
            },
            "description": "Atomic: entry + at least one translation (one per dialect). Requires CONTRIBUTOR."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update entry (CONTRIBUTOR)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"expectedUpdatedAt\": \"{{entryUpdatedAt}}\",\n  \"nawatContent\": \"kunet\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries/{{entryId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries", "{{entryId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Partial update. Renaming regenerates the slug. Contributor edits of published content are gated.\n\n**Requires `expectedUpdatedAt`** — the `updatedAt` you last read. The update is conditional on it, so a row that changed since you loaded it answers 409 EDIT_CONFLICT rather than overwriting the other edit. Run \"Entry detail\" first; it saves the variable."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Publish entry (ADMIN)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries/{{entryId}}/publish",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries", "{{entryId}}", "publish"]
            },
            "description": "Publish. Requires ADMIN."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Unpublish entry (ADMIN)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries/{{entryId}}/unpublish",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries", "{{entryId}}", "unpublish"]
            },
            "description": "Returns a published entry to draft, cascading to its published translations — the mirror of Publish, which cascades to its drafts.\n\nExists because publishing was otherwise one-way: an entry published by mistake could only be resolved by deleting it and creating it again, losing its id, slug and attribution over what is usually a wrong gloss."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete entry (ADMIN)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries/{{entryId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries", "{{entryId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Delete. Requires ADMIN."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Translations (CONTRIBUTOR / ADMIN)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Add translation (CONTRIBUTOR)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"dialectCode\": \"izalco\",\n  \"contentEs\": \"niño\",\n  \"contentEn\": \"child\",\n  \"partOfSpeech\": \"NOUN\",\n  \"phonetic\": \"[ˈkunet]\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries/{{entryId}}/translations",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries", "{{entryId}}", "translations"]
            },
            "description": "One translation per (entry, dialect). Several senses go in a pipe-separated contentEs, not separate rows. Requires CONTRIBUTOR."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update translation (CONTRIBUTOR)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"expectedUpdatedAt\": \"{{translationUpdatedAt}}\",\n  \"contentEs\": \"ni\\u00f1o | muchacho\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/translations/{{translationId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["translations", "{{translationId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Partial. dialectCode is immutable after creation. Requires CONTRIBUTOR.\n\n**Requires `expectedUpdatedAt`** — the `updatedAt` you last read. The update is conditional on it, so a row that changed since you loaded it answers 409 EDIT_CONFLICT rather than overwriting the other edit. Run \"Entry detail\" first; it saves the variable."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete translation (ADMIN)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/translations/{{translationId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["translations", "{{translationId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Delete. Requires ADMIN."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dialects",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List dialects (public)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/dialects",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["dialects"]
            },
            "description": "Reference data, ordered by precedence. Public."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create dialect (ADMIN)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"code\": \"tacuba\",\n  \"nameEs\": \"Nawat de Tacuba\",\n  \"nameEn\": \"Tacuba Nawat\",\n  \"descriptionEs\": \"Variedad del nawat hablada en la comunidad de Tacuba.\",\n  \"descriptionEn\": \"The variety of Nawat spoken in the community of Tacuba.\",\n  \"precedence\": 50\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/dialects",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["dialects"]
            },
            "description": "Both languages required (reference data). precedence optional (defaults to 100). Requires ADMIN."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update dialect (ADMIN)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"precedence\": 45\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/dialects/{{dialectId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["dialects", "{{dialectId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Partial. Requires ADMIN."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete dialect (ADMIN)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/dialects/{{dialectId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["dialects", "{{dialectId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Delete. Blocked if translations reference it (FK). Requires ADMIN."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Admin read surface (CONTRIBUTOR / ADMIN)",
      "description": "The authenticated reads behind the authoring panel. They exist because every public read hardcodes `isPublished: true`, so no other endpoint can return a draft — and because content comes back UNRESOLVED here (contentEs and contentEn side by side), which is what lets an edit form round-trip it.\n\nUnscoped: any CONTRIBUTOR+ sees every entry, because any of them may edit every entry. `?mine=true` narrows to your own authorship by choice.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List entries → saves {{entryId}}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/entries?status=draft&page=1&limit=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "entries"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "draft",
                  "description": "draft (default) | pending-translations | published | all"
                },
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20"
                },
                {
                  "key": "mine",
                  "value": "true",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "Only entries you created, or carrying a translation you created"
                },
                {
                  "key": "q",
                  "value": "takat",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "Case-insensitive substring on nawatContent, not the trigram search"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "`status=pending-translations` is the odd one: it reaches through the relation for PUBLISHED entries holding at least one translation that is not, which is where a dialect added after publishing lands. Those are excluded from the public reads in every locale, so the dialect exists only in the panel until someone publishes the entry again."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Saves the first row's id so the requests below have something to act on.",
                  "let body;",
                  "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = null; }",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('200 with a data array', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(body && body.data, 'no data array').to.be.an('array');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const first = body && body.data && body.data[0];",
                  "if (first) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('entryId', first.id);",
                  "    console.log('entryId =', first.id, '(' + first.nawatContent + ')');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log('No rows for this status — nothing saved.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Entry detail → saves {{entryUpdatedAt}} + {{translationId}}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/entries/{{entryId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "entries", "{{entryId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Unresolved content, both languages, under the same field names the write DTOs use — so a form PATCHes back exactly what it received.\n\n**Run this before either PATCH.** It saves the `updatedAt` values those requests need as their optimistic lock."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// The two PATCH requests need the updatedAt they are editing against.",
                  "// Saved here so the collection can be run top to bottom.",
                  "let body;",
                  "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = null; }",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('200 with an entry', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(body && body.data && body.data.id, 'no entry').to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const entry = body && body.data;",
                  "if (entry) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('entryUpdatedAt', entry.updatedAt);",
                  "    const t = (entry.translations || [])[0];",
                  "    if (t) {",
                  "        pm.environment.set('translationId', t.id);",
                  "        pm.environment.set('translationUpdatedAt', t.updatedAt);",
                  "    } else {",
                  "        console.log('Entry has no translations — translation requests will 404.');",
                  "    }",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Users",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "My profile",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users", "me"]
            },
            "description": "The current user's profile. Any authenticated user; the id comes from the token. Needs a valid Bearer token."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
